  "body": "Hi, I'm testing synapse in a 16.04 ubuntu server container. Tried\n\n```\nadd-apt-repository -s \"https://matrix.org/packages/debian/\"\ngpg --keyserver pgp.mit.edu --recv-keys AD0592FE47F0DF61\napt-get update\n```\n\nand got \n\n```\n...\nErr:6 https://matrix.org/packages/debian xenial Release                                        \n  404  Not Found\n...\nReading package lists... Done                                                                               \nE: The repository 'https://matrix.org/packages/debian xenial Release' does not have a Release file.\nN: Updating from such a repository can't be done securely, and is therefore disabled by default.\nN: See apt-secure(8) manpage for repository creation and user configuration details.\n```\n\nWould you be so kind and update the repo? I'm not a regular ubuntu user so if there's a quick fix on my side, please let me know as well. thanks in advance\n",
